# ============================================================================
# Claudian Starter .gitignore
# Each block cites the gotcha it defends against. See _handoff/GOTCHAS.md.
# Get this file right BEFORE you enable the backup cron: the cron commits
# everything not listed here. See _handoff/SAFETY_POLICY.md part 2.
# ============================================================================

# --- Secrets. Never commit a credential. -----------------------------------
.env
*.env
!.env.example

# G31: Obsidian plugins store API keys in plaintext inside their own
# data.json. Copilot stored an Anthropic key this way. Ignore ALL plugin
# data, not just one plugin. If you want to share your plugin list, commit
# .obsidian/community-plugins.json (a plain name list, no secrets).
.obsidian/plugins/
.obsidian/plugins/*/data.json

# G55: an API key placed in a plugin's environment-variables setting is
# injected into the spawned CLI and silently overrides subscription auth.
# That setting lives in this file. Keep it out of git.
.claudian/claudian-settings.json

# --- Private content. Routed here, never committed. -------------------------
# See wiki/Sensitivity and Security.
_sensitive/
20_personal/finance/
20_personal/_for_review/

# --- Trash and machine caches ----------------------------------------------
.trash/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# G11: Smart Connections writes .ajson index files that reach 80k+ tokens.
# They are machine cache, not content. Never commit them, never read them.
.smart-env/

# --- Per-machine Obsidian state (changes constantly, not useful shared) -----
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json

# --- Machine-local logs and session state ----------------------------------
.claudian/logs/
.claudian/sessions/
_handoff/*.jsonl

# --- Volatile generated files ----------------------------------------------
# These regenerate at every session start and end, so tracking them makes a
# noisy diff on every commit. They hold nothing you cannot rebuild.
# Uncomment to silence the churn. Leaving them tracked is also fine and gives
# you a history of session state.
# _handoff/SESSION_BOOT.md
# _handoff/BOOT_DELTA.md
